rty/bluez" ref="refs/changes/52/381752/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.39" change_id="I06313ffaed48c7bae264ba332a3d03352e58550c" commit="311246e33d004c2f3e33986736d1f66846c97d3b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: core/gatt-client: Fix not return empty array for ReadValue  The response to ReadValue shall be an array which can be empty.  BUG=chromium:643591 TEST=build  Change-Id: I06313ffaed48c7bae264ba332a3d03352e58550c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387527 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="387527" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/27/387527/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.39" change_id="Ibe6eb6da15ea7e3d9beb00e67a5c44fa2e43cf58" commit="d17ed88ffbed9ff7b017c31eb7a46e9b2ee147ad" commit_message="UPSTREAM: core/gatt-client: Don't invalidate Value if length is 0  Reading 0 bytes shall be valid so it shouldn't invalidate the property.  BUG=chromium:643591 TEST=build  Change-Id: Ibe6eb6da15ea7e3d9beb00e67a5c44fa2e43cf58 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/381754 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="381754" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/54/381754/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.39" change_id="Ic9aa668bf13c6f99bd1654d61aa37f47b3956b10" commit="b119bb0da1a2292ea2422e94698977a47b01d946" commit_message="BACKPORT: core/device: Make it more clear random addresses can only be used with LE  Any random address type can only be connected over LE as BR/EDR only support public addresses.  BUG=chromium:643591 TEST=build  Change-Id: Ic9aa668bf13c6f99bd1654d61aa37f47b3956b10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387585 Commit-Ready: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: François Beaufort &lt;fbeaufort@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="387585" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/85/387585/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I092e53f9ac7ab214b3b8cbd45b5b78e971f3ac33" commit="30464ab449533d367a55f6079a9dd99b447914a3" commit_message="BACKPORT: mwifiex: control WLAN and bluetooth coexistence modes  By default our chip will be in spatial coexistence mode. This patch adds a provision to change it to timeshare mode via debugfs command.  Enable timeshare coexistence mode    echo 1 &gt; /sys/kernel/debug/mwifiex/mlan0/timeshare_coex  Go back to spacial coexistence mode    echo 0 &gt; /sys/kernel/debug/mwifiex/mlan0/timeshare_coex  (cherry-pick from commit 46dbe2476c93026b20ddf36c6995e678bd867000 git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/wireless-drivers-next.git master)  BUG=none TEST=With this patch applied, ran tests with Acer Oak chromebook and confirmed bluetooth and WLAN timeshare coex mode works fine. No regressions seen for autotests  Change-Id: I092e53f9ac7ab214b3b8cbd45b5b78e971f3ac33 Signed-off-by: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388091 Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388091" owner_email="akarwar@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/388091/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8b6f8d725deacd2246a27a8f21b355c652a3075c" commit="dbdf59e36126fbb23f38f1fb84bb1d458a85682f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Enable timeshare coexistence mode for BT and Wlan  The chip will be in the spatial coexistence mode by default. This patch enable timeshare coexistence mode for Bluetooth and WLAN by sending the command to the firmware at the time of initalization.  BUG=none TEST=Simultaneous A2DP audio is played on Acer Oak with iperf TCP traffic runnig. Spatial Coex was causing continuous audio glitches. Using TDM mode by default resolved the issue.  Signed-off-by: Karthik D A &lt;karthida@marvell.com&gt; Change-Id: I8b6f8d725deacd2246a27a8f21b355c652a3075c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388092 Commit-Ready: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Tested-by: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388092" owner_email="akarwar@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/388092/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I741d2239e208381db1a0d6263b86f6012fde4ea3" commit="ca79ffe2f466b1927d31294368ee95a301c2370a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: PRIVATE: remove tx_status check for SA tx feedback processing  Currently, when the host receives a enhanced htt stats message, host checks the tx_status from ppdu_stats in enhanced stats message. Host process only if the tx status is zero i.e success.  Due to this check, when there is a complete failure of the packet due to smart antenna training, SA algorithm doesn't know about this failure as we are bailing out much earlier prior to tx feedback parsing. According to FW, he has given a tx feedback with training bit set for failures in training. So there is a mismatch in the packets counter in host and firmware.  This will cause training to not finish. 1. Due to mismatch in the counter and the FW's counter will be exhausted that it won't send any more training feedbacks while the host thinks it has not recived enought train packets to progress in the antenna selection.  So remove this check.  BUG=None TEST=Connect a station after enabling SA algorithm, and check if SA training is happening in high noisy environment  Change-Id: I741d2239e208381db1a0d6263b86f6012fde4ea3 Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/386543 Commit-Ready: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Tested-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Oliver Wen &lt;oliverwen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="386543" owner_email="Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/43/386543/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9131a6c4a4eef2512ab6f6b853caccabcdd7a6b7" commit="1d1b146e81251334f3764340787330940c65f546" commit_message="FROMLIST: mtk-mdp: fix double mutex_unlock  Fix smatch error: media-git/drivers/me